<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Dear Future Sun Devil,&nbsp;</font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Thank you for expressing interest in the <a href="https://newcollege.asu.edu/forensics-science-degree">Forensics (BS)</a> program at Arizona State University. It is the study and application of scientific methods to matters of law. It emphasizes laboratory course work in chemistry and biology, as both areas provide essential experience with techniques commonly used in crime labs. If pursuing a career as a forensic DNA analyst, nine cumulative hours of course work in biochemistry, molecular biology and genetics is required; course work in population genetics is desirable. Students usually look to work as Forensic Science Techs, Pathologists, Medical Scientists, Chemists, and Biological Technicians among many others. By viewing the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/freshman/requirements">major map</a>, you can see the degree requirements outlined for graduation.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Be sure to review our <a href="https://students.asu.edu/freshman/requirements">admission and application requirements</a> for more information about the application process in an easy to follow format. For finding more ways to pay for college, please visit our <a href="https://visit.asu.edu/">scholarships</a> page.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">It's important to find the right fit for your undergraduate program. A great way to learn more about this degree is to register for one of our upcoming information sessions. You can <a href="https://visit.asu.edu/">visit ASU</a> and register for a tour.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">We can’t wait to see you here at West campus! If you have any questions about New College, West campus, or one of our 35 programs, please contact our Recruitment Office through the information listed below. Thank you, and we’ll talk to you soon!&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Kindest Regards</b>,&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">New College Recruitment Team&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">New College of Interdisciplinary Arts and Sciences&nbsp;</font></div><div><font face="arial" color="#990000">Arizona State University, West campus&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><a href="mailto:asknewcollege@asu.edu">asknewcollege@asu.edu</a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:
